Where we go next:
                  The next problem in our sequence should be N-Queens.
                  It builds directly on Word Search but raises the state-management challenge significantly:

Word Search:
          → one moving path through a grid

N-Queens:
        → construct a global configuration row by row
        → maintain column/diagonal constraints
        → aggressive pruning
        → O(1) constraint checks using sets/bitmasks

That will be a particularly useful L6 exercise because we can go beyond the basic solution 
into constraint representation, bitmask optimization, branching-factor reduction, and correctness invariants.

